<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>How to Make a Peanut Butter Sandwich</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --primary-color: #6d4c41;
            --secondary-color: #ffecb3;
            --text-color: #333;
            --bg-color: #f9f9f9;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            color: var(--text-color);
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        header {
            background-color: var(--primary-color);
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 2rem 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
        }

        header h1 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 2.5rem;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 0 1rem;
        }

        .intro {
            background: white;
            padding: 2rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .ingredients {
            background: white;
            padding: 2rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
        }

        .ingredients h2 {
            color: var(--primary-color);
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--secondary-color);
            padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }

        .ingredient-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding: 0;
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
            gap: 1rem;
        }

        .ingredient-list li {
            background: var(--secondary-color);
            padding: 0.5rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .steps {
            background: white;
            padding: 2rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        .step {
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            padding-left: 1rem;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--primary-color);
        }

        .step h3 {
            margin-top: 0;
            color: var(--primary-color);
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 2rem;
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            margin-top: 3rem;
        }

        @media (max-width: 600px) {
            header h1 {
                font-size: 1.8rem;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>The Perfect Peanut Butter Sandwich</h1>
        <p>A simple, delicious guide to making the ultimate snack.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        
        <section class="intro">
            <h2>Introduction</h2>
            <p>Whether you prefer creamy or crunchy, a peanut butter sandwich is a timeless classic. This guide will walk you through the process of assembling a fresh, tasty sandwich in under five minutes.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="ingredients">
            <h2>Ingredients</h2>
            <ul class="ingredient-list">
                <li>2 slices of bread (Whole wheat or white)</li>
                <li>2 tablespoons peanut butter (Creamy or Crunchy)</li>
                <li>1 teaspoon honey or maple syrup (Optional)</li>
                <li>1/2 teaspoon salt (Optional)</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="steps">
            <h2>Instructions</h2>

            <div class="step">
                <h3>1. Prepare Your Bread</h3>
                <p>Take two slices of bread. If you like a toasted texture, lightly toast them in a toaster or pan until golden brown. If you prefer soft bread, simply let them sit at room temperature for 10 minutes.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="step">
                <h3>2. Mix Your Spreads</h3>
                <p>On a small plate, place your peanut butter. Add the honey or maple syrup and a pinch of salt if desired. Mix until smooth and well-combined.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="step">
                <h3>3. Apply the Peanut Butter</h3>
                <p>Spread a generous layer of peanut butter on one slice of bread. Ensure the edges are covered so no peanut butter falls between the bread and your mouth!</p>
            </div>

            <div class="step">
                <h3>4. Add Your Butter</h3>
                <p>Take your second slice of bread and spread a thin layer of the same peanut butter mixture on one side. Alternatively, you can skip the butter if you prefer a lighter sandwich.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="step">
                <h3>5. Assemble and Serve</h3>
                <p>Place the second slice of bread on top of the first, aligning the edges carefully. Press down gently to secure. Slice diagonally or in half if you prefer smaller portions. Enjoy your fresh peanut butter sandwich!</p>
            </div>
        </section>

    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2023 Simple Sandwich Guide</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>

